+Azure AD quickstart (manual steps) — create app, get JWKS & audience
+
+1) Create app registration
+   az ad app create --display-name "aegis-mofn" --identifier-uris "api://aegis-mofn"
+   Note the appId (client id) returned.
+
+2) Create service principal and credential (client secret) if needed
+   az ad sp create --id <appId>
+   az ad sp credential reset --name <appId> --credential-description "aegis-mofn-secret" --years 1
+
+3) JWKS URL and metadata
+   The OpenID Connect metadata URL is:
+     https://login.microsoftonline.com/<TENANT_ID>/v2.0/.well-known/openid-configuration
+   The JWKS URL is value of "jwks_uri" in that document.
+   The audience (OIDC_AUDIENCE) is typically the application URI or client id: e.g., "api://<appId>" or the client id.
+
+4) Set Helm / GitHub secrets:
+   OIDC_JWKS_URL = https://login.microsoftonline.com/<TENANT_ID>/v2.0/.well-known/jwks
+   OIDC_AUDIENCE = "api://<appId>" (or the client id)
+
