+# Orchestrator Usage & Safety Notes
+
+What the orchestrator does (safe-by-default)
+- Validates local tooling presence (gh/kubectl/helm/aws/cosign/jq)
+- Optionally runs terraform plan/apply for evidence infra (requires --tfvars)
+- Triggers build & push images workflow (GH Actions)
+- Bootstraps ArgoCD (if used) and triggers the one-click staging drill workflow
+- Runs MPC pilot manifests in staging cluster (creates mTLS certs and k8s secret)
+- Performs a KMS rotation dry-run (create key + manifest only; alias NOT swapped)
+- Triggers hardened_deploy_pipeline (verify image signatures, MOFN approval, DP check, deploy)
+- Generates an audit packet and uploads to evidence bucket
+
+Important safety constraints
+- Default mode is dry-run. Use --apply to perform live changes and --force if you want to skip interactive confirmations.
+- The orchestrator will never perform alias swaps in KMS; KMS rotation step is a dry-run that creates a new key and manifest. Alias swap must be done manually or via a separate, reviewed workflow after M-of-N approvals.
+- Ensure all repository and cluster secrets are set prior to running in apply mode.
+
+How to run
+- Dry-run:
+  ./ops/orchestrator/one_click_orchestrator.sh --dry-run
+- Apply:
+  ./ops/orchestrator/one_click_orchestrator.sh --apply --tfvars ./terraform/evidence/terraform.tfvars
+
+Operator checklist before apply
+- Confirm GitHub secrets: KUBE_CONFIG_DATA, EVIDENCE_BUCKET, COSIGN_KMS_URI, AWS_* creds, OIDC_JWKS_URL/AUDIENCE, REKOR_SERVER.
+- Confirm you can run kubectl against staging cluster.
+- Ensure cosign and rekor-cli installed on your environment if you need to verify signatures locally.
+
